# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots xinetd with the telnet stanza enabled and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * telnet is ALREADY LISTENING on port 23 when the agent starts, which is
#     what makes "removed /etc/xinetd.d/telnet but never stopped xinetd"
#     detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so stopping xinetd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the live listener must be STOPPED, not just
# disabled on disk. verify.sh also no longer starts sshd for you - the secure
# replacement must be installed AND running.
